1
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:05,956
This is really neat!

2
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,934
When do we eat?

3
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:11,912
First, we have to catch some fish.

4
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:17,868
In order to catch fish, you have to do this.

5
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:20,846
Here we go.

6
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:26,802
That's it.

7
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:30,312
Then drop it into the water.

8
00:00:30,312 --> 00:00:33,008
All of this comes before eating. OK?

9
00:00:33,008 --> 00:00:36,036
How do you know so much about fishing?

10
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:36,936
Grandpa taught me.

11
00:00:36,936 --> 00:00:41,692
We spent a lot of time fishing together.

12
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:51,625
Now, the important thing is to get the hook close to the fish.

13
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:59,875
All right?

14
00:00:59,875 --> 00:01:00,506
Like this.

15
00:01:00,506 --> 00:01:05,915
I think I see some fish right under us, Dad.

16
00:01:05,915 --> 00:01:08,375
Oh, not a chance!

17
00:01:08,375 --> 00:01:11,471
I just saw a big one!

18
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:12,138
Hi, there!

19
00:01:12,138 --> 00:01:12,471
Hi.

20
00:01:12,471 --> 00:01:14,449
What's your name?

21
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:14,792
Albert.

22
00:01:14,792 --> 00:01:16,163
Are you all alone?

23
00:01:16,163 --> 00:01:17,427
Yes, sir.

24
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:20,805
How old are you, Albert?

25
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:21,605
I'm ten.

26
00:01:21,605 --> 00:01:23,883
Where's your father?

27
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:26,861
He's up there at the lodge.

28
00:01:26,861 --> 00:01:30,029
Does he know you're here?

29
00:01:30,029 --> 00:01:30,719
Yes, sir.

30
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:33,517
OK, Robbie, maybe you should watch him.

31
00:01:33,517 --> 00:01:35,067
The water's pretty deep here.

32
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:43,051
I'll watch him, Dad.

33
00:01:43,051 --> 00:01:45,480
What time is it?

34
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,014
It's almost lunchtime, and no fish yet.

35
00:01:48,014 --> 00:01:53,235
I can go up to the lodge for some hot dogs and drinks.

36
00:01:53,235 --> 00:01:54,455
No way!

37
00:01:54,455 --> 00:01:55,230
We're here to catch our lunch.

38
00:01:55,230 --> 00:01:59,785
To catch fish, you need the right magic.

39
00:01:59,785 --> 00:02:00,451
That's right.

40
00:02:00,451 --> 00:02:02,096
I forgot!

41
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:03,296
The right magic.

42
00:02:03,296 --> 00:02:07,846
Do it for Robbie, Dad.

43
00:02:07,846 --> 00:02:08,052
You remember?

44
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:09,052
Sure. Come on.

45
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:14,008
Well, first, you have to turn your hat around like this.

46
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:25,920
Then you close your eyes and say the magic words.

47
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:30,231
Fish, fish, send me a fish.

48
00:02:30,231 --> 00:02:35,438
Fish, fish, send me a fish.... I got one!

49
00:02:35,438 --> 00:02:37,190
See, it works!

50
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,462
It's a big one!

51
00:02:38,462 --> 00:02:48,713
Well, it always worked for me, too.

52
00:02:48,713 --> 00:02:51,504
Grandpa, get the net, please!

53
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:59,438
Dad, you got one, too!

54
00:02:59,438 --> 00:03:00,958
You bet I have!

55
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:02,456
Easy, Philip, easy.

56
00:03:02,456 --> 00:03:03,256
Sorry, Dad.

57
00:03:03,256 --> 00:03:09,212
Well, one more and I've got a pair of boots.

58
00:03:09,212 --> 00:03:10,589
You didn't say the magic words.

59
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:11,476
Robbie's right.

60
00:03:11,476 --> 00:03:13,567
Yes, but you did, and we've got our lunch.

61
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:14,442
Let's build a fire and cook it!

62
00:03:14,442 --> 00:03:16,067
Come on, Albert, you can help us!

63
00:03:16,067 --> 00:03:19,943
I want to stay here and fish.

64
00:03:19,943 --> 00:03:31,435
All right, but be careful.

65
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,768
Is it finished yet?

66
00:03:32,768 --> 00:03:33,768
I think so.

67
00:03:33,768 --> 00:03:38,391
I hope you like your fish well done.

68
00:03:38,391 --> 00:03:39,724
Burned, you mean.

69
00:03:39,724 --> 00:03:53,381
Hey, I'm a doctor, not a chef.

70
00:03:53,381 --> 00:03:55,592
Help! Help! I can't swim!

71
00:03:55,592 --> 00:04:17,605
Dad! Grandpa! He fell in!

72
00:04:17,605 --> 00:04:19,372
Easy does it, Robbie.

73
00:04:19,372 --> 00:04:20,239
That a boy.

74
00:04:20,239 --> 00:04:20,816
That's it.

75
00:04:20,816 --> 00:04:22,103
He's not breathing, Philip!

76
00:04:22,103 --> 00:04:22,677
Robbie, run to the car!

77
00:04:22,677 --> 00:04:25,338
Bring a blanket and my medical bag.

78
00:04:25,338 --> 00:04:25,938
Yes, Dad.

79
00:04:25,938 --> 00:04:37,230
Now, come on, son. Come on, son.

80
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:37,790
Breathe, Albert!
